# Part II – Enterprise Business Domains

## 9. Business Domain Architecture

### 9.1 Overview

The Essentials Mart platform is organised into independent business domains.

Each domain represents a distinct business capability with clearly defined responsibilities, ownership boundaries, enterprise events, and data models.

A domain owns its data.

A domain exposes behaviour.

A domain collaborates with other domains through well-defined interfaces and events.

No domain should become responsible for functionality that belongs to another domain.

This separation ensures scalability, maintainability, explainability, and future modularisation.

---

# 10. Enterprise Domain Catalogue

The platform currently consists of thirteen primary business domains.

| Domain | Primary Responsibility |
|---------|------------------------|
| User | Individual customer lifecycle and experience |
| Identity & Access | Authentication, authorisation and security |
| Commerce | Shopping lifecycle from Cart to Order |
| Product Intelligence | Products, pricing, catalogues and recommendations |
| Retail Intelligence | Stores, operations and retailer optimisation |
| Household | Household collaboration and shared resources |
| Community | Club Plans and collaborative purchasing |
| Inventory Intelligence | Stock visibility, Smart Pantry and replenishment |
| Engagement Intelligence | Rewards, loyalty, reactivation and customer engagement |
| Customer Intelligence | Learning engine, reviews, feedback and behavioural understanding |
| AI Society | Intelligent agents and orchestration |
| Enterprise | ERP, reporting and operational intelligence |
| System | Notifications, audit, configuration and platform infrastructure |

## 10.1 User Domain

### Purpose

The User Domain manages the complete lifecycle of an individual customer within the Essentials Mart platform.

Every interaction begins with a user.

The platform earns trust at the individual level before encouraging participation in households, communities, and other collaborative experiences.

The User Domain is therefore the primary entry point into the platform.

---

### Responsibilities

The User Domain is responsible for:

- User profiles
- Customer preferences
- Personal shopping behaviour
- Walk Mode experience
- User onboarding
- User settings
- Personal favourites
- Personal shopping history
- Personal notification preferences
- Individual goals and preferences

---

### Owns

The User Domain owns:

- User
- User Profile
- Preferences
- Shopping Preferences
- Saved Items
- Favourite Products
- Recently Viewed Products
- Personal Shopping Lists
- Personal Activity Timeline

---

### Does Not Own

The User Domain does not own:

- Authentication (Identity & Access)
- Household membership (Household)
- Orders (Commerce)
- Product catalogue (Product Intelligence)
- Inventory (Inventory Intelligence)
- Rewards (Engagement Intelligence)

---

### Primary Events

The User Domain publishes events including:

- User Registered
- User Updated
- Walk Mode Activated
- Preferences Updated
- Favourite Added
- Favourite Removed
- Shopping List Created
- Shopping List Updated

---

### Consumes Events

The User Domain listens to events from:

- Identity & Access
- Commerce
- Engagement Intelligence
- Customer Intelligence

---

### Collaborates With

The User Domain collaborates closely with:

- Household
- Commerce
- Engagement Intelligence
- Customer Intelligence
- AI Society

---

### AI Society Relationship

Primary AI Agent:

**User Experience Agent**

Responsibilities include:

- Understanding customer behaviour
- Learning preferences
- Personalising recommendations
- Improving onboarding
- Supporting Walk Mode
- Identifying friction within the user journey

The User Experience Agent does not make purchasing decisions on behalf of the customer.

It provides recommendations while preserving customer autonomy.

---

### Architectural Principles

The User Domain must always remain:

- customer-first;
- privacy-aware;
- explainable;
- independently scalable;
- independent of retail operations.

No other domain may modify User-owned information directly.

Changes must occur through User Domain services.

---

### Success Criteria

The User Domain succeeds when:

- new users quickly understand the platform;
- customers trust the platform;
- users naturally transition into household participation;
- friction throughout the user journey continually decreases.
---
## 10.2 Household Domain

### Purpose

The Household Domain manages collaborative living by allowing multiple users to organise, plan, purchase, budget and manage household resources together.

While every customer begins as an individual, the long-term objective of the platform is to help users transition naturally into household participation where AI can deliver significantly greater value through shared intelligence, collaboration and planning.

The Household Domain represents the platform's primary collaborative environment.

---

### Responsibilities

The Household Domain is responsible for:

- Household creation
- Household membership
- Household roles and permissions
- Household settings
- Household Wallet
- Shared shopping lists
- Smart Pantry ownership
- Household budgets
- Household goals
- Household planning
- Household activity timeline

---

### Owns

The Household Domain owns:

- Household
- Household Member
- Household Role
- Household Wallet
- Household Budget
- Shared Shopping Lists
- Household Preferences
- Household Goals
- Household Timeline

---

### Does Not Own

The Household Domain does not own:

- User authentication (Identity & Access)
- Individual user profiles (User)
- Orders (Commerce)
- Product catalogue (Product Intelligence)
- Stock management (Inventory Intelligence)
- Loyalty rewards (Engagement Intelligence)

---

### Primary Events

The Household Domain publishes events including:

- Household Created
- Household Updated
- Member Invited
- Member Joined
- Member Removed
- Household Wallet Created
- Household Budget Updated
- Shared Shopping List Created
- Household Goal Created

---

### Consumes Events

The Household Domain listens to events from:

- User
- Commerce
- Community
- Inventory Intelligence
- Customer Intelligence

---

### Collaborates With

The Household Domain collaborates closely with:

- User
- Commerce
- Community
- Inventory Intelligence
- AI Society
- Customer Intelligence

---

### AI Society Relationship

Primary AI Agent:

**Household Intelligence Agent**

Responsibilities include:

- Coordinating household activities
- Understanding household routines
- Supporting Household Wallet decisions
- Managing Smart Pantry intelligence
- Monitoring household consumption patterns
- Recommending collaborative purchasing opportunities
- Supporting long-term household planning

The Household Intelligence Agent assists household members but never removes their authority over household decisions.

---

### Architectural Principles

The Household Domain must:

- promote collaboration;
- preserve transparency between members;
- protect household privacy;
- support multiple household structures;
- remain independent of commerce implementation.

A household may contain one or many users.

A user may belong to multiple households only where explicitly permitted by future business rules.

---

### Success Criteria

The Household Domain succeeds when:

- users naturally choose to create households;
- collaboration reduces shopping effort;
- Household Wallet simplifies budgeting;
- Smart Pantry becomes increasingly accurate;
- households feel genuinely supported rather than merely managed.

## 10.3 Identity & Access Domain

### Purpose

The Identity & Access Domain establishes, verifies and protects the identity of every user interacting with the Essentials Mart platform.

Its responsibility is to ensure that every authenticated action is secure, traceable and appropriately authorised while providing a frictionless customer experience.

This domain forms the security foundation of the entire platform.

---

### Responsibilities

The Identity & Access Domain is responsible for:

- User authentication
- User authorisation
- Account verification
- Session management
- Device management
- Password management
- Multi-factor authentication
- Role management
- Permission management
- Security auditing
- Account recovery

---

### Owns

The Identity & Access Domain owns:

- Authentication Credentials
- Sessions
- Refresh Tokens
- Device Registrations
- Login History
- Roles
- Permissions
- Security Policies
- Account Verification Status

---

### Does Not Own

The Identity & Access Domain does not own:

- User profile information (User)
- Household membership (Household)
- Orders (Commerce)
- Customer preferences (User)
- Rewards (Engagement Intelligence)

---

### Primary Events

The Identity & Access Domain publishes events including:

- User Authenticated
- User Logged Out
- Session Created
- Session Expired
- Device Registered
- Device Removed
- Password Changed
- Role Assigned
- Permission Updated
- Account Verified

---

### Consumes Events

The Identity & Access Domain listens to events from:

- User
- System

---

### Collaborates With

The Identity & Access Domain collaborates with every domain that requires authenticated access.

Its strongest relationships are with:

- User
- Household
- Commerce
- Enterprise
- System

---

### AI Society Relationship

Primary AI Agent:

**Security Intelligence Agent**

Responsibilities include:

- Detecting unusual login behaviour
- Monitoring suspicious authentication attempts
- Identifying potential account compromise
- Recommending additional verification where necessary
- Supporting fraud prevention

The Security Intelligence Agent may recommend security actions but must never permanently deny customer access without explicit platform security policies.

---

### Architectural Principles

The Identity & Access Domain must:

- minimise customer friction;
- maximise platform security;
- support zero-trust architecture principles;
- remain independently scalable;
- provide complete auditability.

Authentication determines identity.

Authorisation determines capability.

These responsibilities must never be mixed.

---

### Success Criteria

The Identity & Access Domain succeeds when:

- customers authenticate effortlessly;
- unauthorised access is prevented;
- security events are fully traceable;
- authentication remains reliable under scale;
- customer trust in platform security continues to increase.

## 10.4 Commerce Domain

### Purpose

The Commerce Domain is responsible for transforming customer purchase decisions into trusted, secure and efficient commercial transactions.

Unlike traditional retail systems, the Commerce Domain does not attempt to influence customer decisions. Instead, it provides the services required to convert an already-made purchasing decision into successful fulfilment while preserving transparency, customer autonomy and trust.

The Commerce Domain represents the transactional backbone of the Essentials Mart platform.

---

### Responsibilities

The Commerce Domain is responsible for:

- Shopping Cart management
- Checkout
- Order creation
- Order lifecycle management
- Payment orchestration
- Household Wallet payment integration
- Club Plan payment coordination
- Delivery option selection
- Collection option selection
- Order fulfilment orchestration
- Returns initiation
- Refund initiation
- Order status tracking

---

### Owns

The Commerce Domain owns:

- Cart
- Cart Item
- Checkout Session
- Order
- Order Item
- Payment Transaction
- Delivery Selection
- Collection Selection
- Fulfilment Request
- Return Request
- Refund Request

---

### Does Not Own

The Commerce Domain does not own:

- User identity (Identity & Access)
- Customer profiles (User)
- Household membership (Household)
- Product catalogue (Product Intelligence)
- Inventory availability (Inventory Intelligence)
- Promotions and rewards (Engagement Intelligence)
- Shopping experiences (Shopping Experience Platform)

---

### Primary Events

The Commerce Domain publishes events including:

- Cart Created
- Cart Updated
- Checkout Started
- Checkout Completed
- Order Created
- Order Confirmed
- Payment Authorised
- Payment Failed
- Order Cancelled
- Order Fulfilled
- Return Requested
- Refund Issued

---

### Consumes Events

The Commerce Domain listens to events from:

- User
- Household
- Product Intelligence
- Inventory Intelligence
- Engagement Intelligence
- Enterprise
- Customer Intelligence

---

### Collaborates With

The Commerce Domain collaborates closely with:

- Household
- Inventory Intelligence
- Product Intelligence
- Engagement Intelligence
- Customer Intelligence
- Enterprise
- AI Society

---

### AI Society Relationship

Primary AI Agent:

**Commerce Intelligence Agent**

Responsibilities include:

- Coordinating commercial workflows
- Monitoring transaction integrity
- Explaining checkout information
- Assisting with delivery choices
- Supporting payment guidance
- Coordinating fulfilment with other AI agents

The Commerce Intelligence Agent does not make purchasing decisions for customers.

Its role is to simplify commerce while preserving complete customer control.

---

### Architectural Principles

The Commerce Domain must:

- remain transaction-focused;
- never manipulate purchasing behaviour;
- remain independent of shopping experiences;
- provide complete transactional traceability;
- support multiple payment methods;
- remain horizontally scalable.

Commerce begins when a customer intentionally places an item into a cart.

Everything before Cart belongs to the Shopping Experience Platform.

---

### Success Criteria

The Commerce Domain succeeds when:

- checkout is frictionless;
- transactions are trustworthy;
- fulfilment is reliable;
- payments are secure;
- customers retain confidence throughout the purchasing process.

---

### Domain Boundary

The Commerce Domain owns transactional execution.

The Shopping Experience Platform owns customer shopping experiences.

Shopping experiences include:

- Walk Mode
- Browse Mode
- Express Mode
- AI Companion interactions
- Context awareness
- Navigation

These experiences may generate shopping decisions but never execute commercial transactions directly.

All purchasing decisions enter Commerce through the Cart.

## 10.5 Product Intelligence Domain

### Purpose

The Product Intelligence Domain is responsible for managing, enriching and continuously evolving the knowledge associated with every product available on the Essentials Mart platform.

Rather than treating products as simple catalogue entries, this domain establishes each product as an intelligent digital asset capable of supporting commerce, artificial intelligence, household decision-making, health awareness, operational excellence and immersive shopping experiences.

The Product Intelligence Domain serves as the single source of truth for all product knowledge across the enterprise.

---

### Responsibilities

The Product Intelligence Domain is responsible for:

- Product catalogue management
- Product specifications
- Brand management
- Category management
- Nutritional information
- Ingredient information
- Allergen information
- Dietary suitability
- Product attributes
- Product media
- Product documentation
- Product relationships
- Product substitutions
- Product compatibility
- Recipe associations
- Sustainability information
- Packaging information
- Digital product assets
- Product semantic knowledge

---

### Owns

The Product Intelligence Domain owns:

