---

### Collaborates With

The Product Intelligence Domain collaborates closely with:

- Commerce
- Inventory Intelligence
- Retail Intelligence
- Customer Intelligence
- Household
- AI Society

---

### AI Society Relationship

Primary AI Agent:

**Product Intelligence Agent**

Responsibilities include:

- Explaining products in natural language
- Comparing similar products
- Recommending appropriate substitutes
- Understanding customer questions
- Enriching product knowledge
- Supporting Walk Mode interactions
- Assisting other AI agents with product reasoning

The Product Intelligence Agent explains products.

It never decides what customers should purchase.

---

### Architectural Principles

The Product Intelligence Domain must:

- maintain a single authoritative product record;
- separate knowledge from inventory;
- separate knowledge from pricing;
- continuously enrich product information;
- remain explainable;
- support multilingual product understanding;
- support future global product catalogues.

Every product should become increasingly intelligent as the platform learns more about it.

---

### Success Criteria

The Product Intelligence Domain succeeds when:

- every product is consistently understood across the platform;
- AI agents accurately reason about products;
- customers receive trustworthy product information;
- substitutions remain reliable;
- product knowledge continuously improves.

---

### Digital Product Vision

Every product within Essentials Mart should evolve into a rich digital representation rather than a simple catalogue record.

Over time, products may include:

- realistic digital models for Walk Mode;
- manufacturer-provided assets;
- AI-generated semantic understanding;
- nutritional intelligence;
- household suitability profiles;
- recipe compatibility;
- sustainability indicators;
- historical knowledge;
- multilingual descriptions.

Products are not merely items that can be purchased.

They become intelligent digital entities that support the entire Household Care Platform.

# 11. Domain Philosophy

Every business capability belongs to one and only one primary domain.

Domains communicate through events rather than sharing responsibility.

Each domain should answer one business question exceptionally well.

Examples:

User Domain

"Who is this customer?"

Household Domain

"Which household is this person part of?"

Commerce Domain

"What is this customer trying to purchase?"

Inventory Intelligence

"Can the requested products be fulfilled?"

AI Society

"What should happen next?"

Customer Intelligence

"What have we learned?"

Enterprise

"How should the business respond?"

---

# 12. Enterprise Domain Relationships

The User domain is the entry point into the platform.

Every journey begins with an individual.

The Household domain extends the individual experience into collaborative household management.

Commerce manages shopping activities.

Product Intelligence provides commercial knowledge.

Inventory Intelligence determines product availability.

Community enables collaborative purchasing.

Customer Intelligence continuously learns from every interaction.

Engagement Intelligence strengthens long-term customer relationships.

AI Society coordinates intelligent decision making across all domains.

Enterprise transforms operational data into business intelligence.

System provides the infrastructure required to support all domains.

---

# 13. Domain Ownership Principles

Every domain must satisfy the following ownership rules.

• Own its own data.

• Own its own business rules.

• Own its own events.

• Never duplicate another domain's responsibilities.

• Expose services rather than internal implementation.

• Remain independently scalable.

These principles are mandatory throughout the platform.

---

# 14. Domain Dependency Rules

Dependencies should always move toward business collaboration rather than business ownership.

For example:

User
↓

Household
↓

Commerce
↓

Inventory Intelligence
↓

Order

Customer Intelligence may observe every domain.

AI Society may coordinate every domain.

Enterprise may analyse every domain.

However, observation does not imply ownership.

Ownership always remains within the originating domain.

---

